{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546658183,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb1fa78ffe4VCKRa9h8ICYkK","part":{"id":"prt_1d350e9c5002EiUtQHBS4f6arz","sessionID":"ses_e2cb1fa78ffe4VCKRa9h8ICYkK","messageID":"msg_1d350cfd5001QPGboQlnNEn2yY","type":"text","text":"T023 is applied and every check passes. Only `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs` changed.\n\nWhat changed in that file:\n1. Imported `restoreTurn` and `statusSnapshot` from `./worktree-restore.mjs`, and dropped the now-unused `rmSync` import.\n2. `statusPaths()` now delegates to `statusSnapshot(REPO_ROOT)`.\n3. `runTurn` calls `restoreTurn({ cwd: REPO_ROOT, before: before.status })` for a live run, keeps `changed.length === 0` for a dry run, and takes `restored` from the result.\n4. Added `leftoverPaths` to the run line only when non-empty, and to the `restore_failed` refusal.\n5. Removed `pathIsTracked`, `restorePath` and `restorePaths`.\n\nVerify output:\n\n```\nnode --check exit=0\nrg removed exit=1        (no output: no restorePath or pathIsTracked match)\n2                        (rg -c \"restoreTurn\")\nrg restoreTurn exit=0\n```\n\n```\n RUN  v4.1.12 /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\n```\n\nI also ran `node \"$R\" --list g2` as an import smoke check, exit 0.\n\nNothing was left undone. I did not tick the checkbox, did not edit tasks.md, and made no commit, push or other git state change. The scoped diff is 18 insertions and 38 deletions in that one file. Nothing is blocked on the operator, and no residual risk is known.","time":{"start":1794546657733,"end":1794546658183}}}
